      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "function useSearch(query: string) {\n  const [result, setResult] = React.useState([]);\n  const [status, setStatus] =\n    React.useState<\"idle\" | \"loading\" | \"error\">(\"idle\");\n\n  React.useEffect(() => {\n    if (!query.trim()) {\n      setResult([]);\n      return;\n    }\n\n    const controller = new AbortController();\n    const timer = window.setTimeout(async () => {\n      setStatus(\"loading\");\n\n      try {\n        const res = await fetch(\n          `/api/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(query)}`,\n          { signal: controller.signal }\n        );\n\n        if (!res.ok) throw new Error(\"Search failed\");\n        setResult(await res.json());\n        setStatus(\"idle\");\n      } catch (error) {\n        if (!controller.signal.aborted) setStatus(\"error\");\n      }\n    }, 250);\n\n    return () => {\n      clearTimeout(timer);\n      controller.abort();\n    };\n  }, [query]);\n\n  return { result, status };\n}\n\nTrade-offs:\n• debounce lowers traffic but adds input-to-result latency\n• cancellation prevents stale responses\n• server cache library is better when dedupe, retry, and cache matter\n• useDeferredValue helps rendering pressure; it does not debounce network calls",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "function useSearch(query: string) {\n  const [result, setResult] = React.useState([]);\n  const [status, setStatus] =\n    React.useState<\"idle\" | \"loading\" | \"error\">(\"idle\");\n\n  React.useEffect(() => {\n    if (!query.trim()) {\n      setResult([]);\n      return;\n    }\n\n    const controller = new AbortController();\n    const timer = window.setTimeout(async () => {\n      setStatus(\"loading\");\n\n      try {\n        const res = await fetch(\n          `/api/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(query)}`,\n          { signal: controller.signal }\n        );\n\n        if (!res.ok) throw new Error(\"Search failed\");\n        setResult(await res.json());\n        setStatus(\"idle\");\n      } catch (error) {\n        if (!controller.signal.aborted) setStatus(\"error\");\n      }\n    }, 250);\n\n    return () => {\n      clearTimeout(timer);\n      controller.abort();\n    };\n  }, [query]);\n\n  return { result, status };\n}\n\nTrade-offs:\n• debounce lowers traffic but adds input-to-result latency\n• cancellation prevents stale responses\n• server cache library is better when dedupe, retry, and cache matter\n• useDeferredValue helps rendering pressure; it does not debounce network calls",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
