      "text": "7. Trade-off matrix to say out loud",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "7. Trade-off matrix to say out loud",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "a35b8f23dd3e",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 2108,
      "width": 1680,
      "height": 276.25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ah",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 44,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 391431145,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784909313040,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "Decision                 Choose A when...                              Choose B when...                           Key interview line\n\nLocal state vs global      isolated UI / short lifetime                  shared cross-route workflow              “I keep state close until sharing pressure appears.”\nContext vs store           low-frequency stable values                   frequent selective updates               “Context broadcasts; stores allow subscriptions.”\nREST vs GraphQL            simple resources / HTTP caching               many client-shaped views                  “GraphQL shifts complexity to schema and cache.”\nSSE vs WebSocket           server→client streaming, simpler ops          bidirectional low-latency events          “SSE is enough for token streaming.”\nPolling vs subscription    simple, tolerant of latency                   near-real-time updates                    “Start simple, upgrade when freshness SLO requires it.”\nCSR vs SSR                 authenticated app, rich interaction           SEO / fast first content                  “Use hybrid rendering per route.”\nMemoization                measured expensive recomputation              cheap values / unstable props             “Memoization has cognitive and memory cost.”\nVirtualization             large lists and bounded row geometry          small lists / print / browser find        “Optimize DOM count, not only data count.”\nOptimistic update          reversible, high-confidence mutation          destructive / conflict-prone action       “Rollback and conflict UX are part of the design.”\nDesign-system wrapper      consistency and migration leverage            highly specialized product UI             “Escape hatches must be intentional, not accidental.”\nUnit vs E2E                logic and fast diagnostics                    confidence in critical journeys           “Use the test pyramid by failure cost, not dogma.”",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Decision                 Choose A when...                              Choose B when...                           Key interview line\n\nLocal state vs global      isolated UI / short lifetime                  shared cross-route workflow              “I keep state close until sharing pressure appears.”\nContext vs store           low-frequency stable values                   frequent selective updates               “Context broadcasts; stores allow subscriptions.”\nREST vs GraphQL            simple resources / HTTP caching               many client-shaped views                  “GraphQL shifts complexity to schema and cache.”\nSSE vs WebSocket           server→client streaming, simpler ops          bidirectional low-latency events          “SSE is enough for token streaming.”\nPolling vs subscription    simple, tolerant of latency                   near-real-time updates                    “Start simple, upgrade when freshness SLO requires it.”\nCSR vs SSR                 authenticated app, rich interaction           SEO / fast first content                  “Use hybrid rendering per route.”\nMemoization                measured expensive recomputation              cheap values / unstable props             “Memoization has cognitive and memory cost.”\nVirtualization             large lists and bounded row geometry          small lists / print / browser find        “Optimize DOM count, not only data count.”\nOptimistic update          reversible, high-confidence mutation          destructive / conflict-prone action       “Rollback and conflict UX are part of the design.”\nDesign-system wrapper      consistency and migration leverage            highly specialized product UI             “Escape hatches must be intentional, not accidental.”\nUnit vs E2E                logic and fast diagnostics                    confidence in critical journeys           “Use the test pyramid by failure cost, not dogma.”",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
