    {
      "id": "fdc3c5c28d74",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 54.5390625,
      "y": 2561.6953125,
      "width": 579.2066040039062,
      "height": 807.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ak",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 47,
      "version": 42,
      "versionNonce": 989148871,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784909432412,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "Unit\n• reducer ignores stale request IDs\n• token buffering flushes correctly\n• citation parser rejects malformed input\n• retry/backoff policy\n\nComponent\n• submit button disabled while invalid\n• Escape cancels generation\n• focus moves to new response status\n• screen reader gets batched live-region updates\n• unsafe HTML is rendered as text or sanitized\n\nIntegration\n• MSW mocks token stream, disconnect, reconnect, 429, 500\n• duplicate events remain idempotent\n• optimistic feedback rolls back on failure\n• cache invalidation after title update\n\nE2E\n• send → stream → cancel → retry\n• open citation in accessible dialog\n• reconnect resumes without duplicate text\n• keyboard-only conversation flow\n\nVisual / performance\n• message variants and tool cards\n• 1,000-message thread remains responsive\n• track INP, long tasks, dropped frames\n\nExample reducer test:\nit(\"ignores stale tokens\", () => {\n  const state = { status: \"streaming\", text: \"A\", requestId: \"new\" };\n  const next = reducer(state, {\n    type: \"TOKEN\", requestId: \"old\", token: \"B\"\n  });\n  expect(next.text).toBe(\"A\");\n});",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Unit\n• reducer ignores stale request IDs\n• token buffering flushes correctly\n• citation parser rejects malformed input\n• retry/backoff policy\n\nComponent\n• submit button disabled while invalid\n• Escape cancels generation\n• focus moves to new response status\n• screen reader gets batched live-region updates\n• unsafe HTML is rendered as text or sanitized\n\nIntegration\n• MSW mocks token stream, disconnect, reconnect, 429, 500\n• duplicate events remain idempotent\n• optimistic feedback rolls back on failure\n• cache invalidation after title update\n\nE2E\n• send → stream → cancel → retry\n• open citation in accessible dialog\n• reconnect resumes without duplicate text\n• keyboard-only conversation flow\n\nVisual / performance\n• message variants and tool cards\n• 1,000-message thread remains responsive\n• track INP, long tasks, dropped frames\n\nExample reducer test:\nit(\"ignores stale tokens\", () => {\n  const state = { status: \"streaming\", text: \"A\", requestId: \"new\" };\n  const next = reducer(state, {\n    type: \"TOKEN\", requestId: \"old\", token: \"B\"\n  });\n  expect(next.text).toBe(\"A\");\n});",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
