      "fontSize": 26,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "10. Real architectural trade-off story framework",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "10. Real architectural trade-off story framework",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "8db9221cc73a",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 3688,
      "width": 1680,
      "height": 488.75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 53,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 51527591,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784909313040,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "Use one concrete story from your LinkedIn / MLOps work.\n\nSituation\nModel Foundry pages aggregated online and offline model metrics, but initial page loads were 12–15 seconds.\n\nDecision\nMove from a single blocking aggregate request to staged loading:\n1. render model identity and ownership first\n2. fetch summary metrics in parallel\n3. lazy-load expensive tabs\n4. cache stable metadata\n5. add request cancellation and stale-response guards\n\nTrade-off\n• Benefit: time-to-useful-content improved substantially\n• Cost: more frontend state transitions, partial-loading UX, and cache invalidation complexity\n• Rejected alternative: preload every tab because it preserved simplicity but wasted network and delayed first interaction\n• Guardrails: skeletons, error boundaries per section, tracing by endpoint, p95 latency dashboards\n• Result: online active-model page improved to under ~4 seconds; registered-model path to ~1 second\n\nHow to communicate:\n“I chose progressive disclosure over one-shot consistency. The UI became more complex,\nbut users could act sooner, and failures became isolated instead of blocking the whole page.”",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Use one concrete story from your LinkedIn / MLOps work.\n\nSituation\nModel Foundry pages aggregated online and offline model metrics, but initial page loads were 12–15 seconds.\n\nDecision\nMove from a single blocking aggregate request to staged loading:\n1. render model identity and ownership first\n2. fetch summary metrics in parallel\n3. lazy-load expensive tabs\n4. cache stable metadata\n5. add request cancellation and stale-response guards\n\nTrade-off\n• Benefit: time-to-useful-content improved substantially\n• Cost: more frontend state transitions, partial-loading UX, and cache invalidation complexity\n• Rejected alternative: preload every tab because it preserved simplicity but wasted network and delayed first interaction\n• Guardrails: skeletons, error boundaries per section, tracing by endpoint, p95 latency dashboards\n• Result: online active-model page improved to under ~4 seconds; registered-model path to ~1 second\n\nHow to communicate:\n“I chose progressive disclosure over one-shot consistency. The UI became more complex,\nbut users could act sooner, and failures became isolated instead of blocking the whole page.”",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
